<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 170,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 170,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 100,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 30,000 of Canadian wheat, 40,000 of Australian wheat and 20,000 of U.S. barley in its weekly tender.</p>
<p>They are all for September shipments. The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> COUNTRY    QUANTITY</p>
<p> U.S.	 100,000   Western White	    30,000</p>
<p>			    Dark Northern Spring   50,000</p>
<p>			    Hard Red Winter</p>
<p>			    (Protein 13 percent)   10,000</p>
<p>			    Feed			 10,000</p>
<p> Canada     30,000    1CW			  30,000</p>
<p> Australia  40,000    Standard White	   20,000</p>
<p>			    Prime Hard		 20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> U.S.	  20,000   Feed			 20,000</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
